From f2b496b0a7a96cc0e2f5c77768d303e2f53d832f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:28:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): a jstack brief opens as what it says: its one
 line, chips, what is out of bounds, a checklist, and the Markdown one click
 away

"Open brief" showed the brief file as one block of monospace text. It now draws the brief in
one column: its one line, then Size, Review, Playbook, Pull request and Home as chips, then
Do not touch (or a scout's Out of bounds) as a band directly under them, then the brief's own
lines in its order, each under an 11px label: Task quoted, Done when a checklist, Questions
numbered, Where as file chips, Builds on and Follows as links. Decisions, Design, Skills, a
scout's lines and jbus's own lines fold under "More", each `## ` section (Report, Result,
Review) is its own fold, and "Markdown" shows the file as jbus keeps it.

The parse reads jbus's label grammar and the line names of jstack's brief and scout request
templates, jbus's own lines and `Follows:`, one registry giving each its place and look. A
line no template names is kept as written, with the list under it, where it was written.

A Builds on or Follows link to a row the tree has closes the dialog, unfolds the row's project,
lifts its home's cap and selects the row, which takes the focus; it stays the tree's selection
until the route moves. A row the tree no longer has says "not in the tree".

The dialog keeps to 13/400 and 11/400: DialogTitle and DialogDescription take a compact size
and Button a row size. Its one accent, sky, is a theme colour (jstack-link) on the links only.
The approve flow is as it was: the sha line, Close and "Approve this brief", none for a scout.
